":null}],"state":"closed","locked":false,"assignee":null,"assignees":[],"milestone":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sqlalchemy/sqlalchemy/milestones/70","html_url":"https://github.com/sqlalchemy/sqlalchemy/milestone/70","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sqlalchemy/sqlalchemy/milestones/70/labels","id":3850654,"node_id":"MDk6TWlsZXN0b25lMzg1MDY1NA==","number":70,"title":"1.1.xx","description":"","creator":{"login":"sqlalchemy-bot","id":36047385,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM2MDQ3Mzg1","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/36047385?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/sqlalchemy-bot","html_url":"https://github.com/sqlalchemy-bot","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sqlalchemy-bot/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sqlalchemy-bot/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sqlalchemy-bot/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sqlalchemy-bot/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sqlalchemy-bot/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sqlalchemy-bot/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sqlalchemy-bot/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sqlalchemy-bot/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sqlalchemy-bot/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"open_issues":0,"closed_issues":93,"state":"closed","created_at":"2018-11-27T04:29:29Z","updated_at":"2020-05-19T11:42:50Z","due_on":null,"closed_at":"2018-11-28T16:50:01Z"},"comments":11,"created_at":"2017-03-06T14:04:50Z","updated_at":"2017-03-20T13:09:13Z","closed_at":"2017-03-07T00:13:01Z","author_association":"COLLABORATOR","type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"**Migrated issue, originally created by Bartłomiej Biernacki ([@pax0r](https://github.com/pax0r))**\n\nI found a small memory leak when using many savepoints to the same DB.\n\nConsider this code example:\n\n```\nsession = create_session()\n\nfor _ in range(0, 5000):\n    session.begin_nested()\n    session.execute(\n        sa.insert(Test).values(name='test'))\n    session.commit()\n\nsession.commit()\nsession.close()\n```\n\nAfter this we can observe 5000 strings with savepoints names in memory. \n\nDiging deeply into it I found that function `sql/compiler.py:format_savepoint` saves savepoint name to `self._strings`. By default savepoint names are unique for each nested transaction so saving them for future use is redundant and each new savepoint name stays in memory.\n\nMy proposition is to change the function, so savepoint name won't be saved:\n\n```\n    def format_savepoint(self, savepoint, name=None):\n        value = name or savepoint.ident\n        if self._requires_quotes(value):\n            return self.quote_identifier(value)\n        return value\n```\n\nComplete code example for reproducing bug in attachment.\n\n----------------------------------------\nAttachments: [sql_alchemy_poc.py](../wiki/imported_issue_attachments/3931/sql_alchemy_poc.py)\n\n","closed_by":{"login":"sqlalchemy-bot","id":36047385,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM2MDQ3Mzg1","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/36047385?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/sqlalchemy-bot","html_url":"https://github.com/sqlalchemy-bot","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sqlalchemy-bot/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sqlalchemy-bot/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sqlalchemy-bot/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sqlalchemy-bot/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sqlalchemy-bot/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sqlalchemy-bot/orgs","repos_u